This add-on comes unchanged from the SEED-Emulator repository:

    tools/InternetMap2/plugin/submit_event/

It is the add-on the Morris worm and Mirai examples there use to show
infected machines on the Internet Map. With it installed, a machine calls

    bash /map-plugins/submit_event.sh -a flash        (or highlight, or restore)

and the map flashes that machine. The map's server looks for this folder at
/usr/src/app/plugin/submit_event inside itself, so it is put there when the
lab is built. It only has to be switched on once the lab is up:

    curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
         -d '{"name": "submit_event"}' http://localhost:8082/api/v1/install
